%N A401081 Number of distinct tangency polynomials of meandric permutations of length n.
%C A401081 For a permutation pi, the coefficient of x^k in its tangency polynomial counts the number of singular meanders realizing pi with exactly k tangencies. The sequence counts distinct nonzero tangency polynomials of meandric permutations. Equivalently, it counts distinct tangency polynomials with constant term 1.
%H A401081 Yury Belousov, <a href="https://github.com/YuryBelousov/s_meandric">C++ code for generating the sequence</a>, GitHub.
%H A401081 Yury Belousov and Viktoriia Georgievskaia, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.30068">S-meandric Permutations and Tangency Polynomials</a>, arXiv:2609.30068 [math.CO], 2026.
%F A401081 a(n) ~ exp(Pi*sqrt(2*n/3))/(2*Pi*sqrt(2*n)).
%e A401081 a(3) = 2. The two distinct polynomials are (1+x)^3 and 1+3*x^2.
%Y A401081 Cf. A393122, A400881, A005316, A401079.
